<title>ITALY: Italy's Naples sees June CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Naples sees June CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>NAPLES, Italy 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Naples said its June consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month on month and 1.9 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In May, Naples' inflation rate was 0.0 percent month on month and 2.1 percent year on year.</p>
<p>Naples is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data Friday and Monday. The city's CPI weighs 6.64 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>The following is the breakdown of the price changes:</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to May 1997)</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		  +0.1    (0.0)    +1.9    (2.1)</p>
<p>    Food				0.0    (0.1)    +1.5    (2.0)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	 0.0    (0.0)    +1.3    (1.4)</p>
<p>    Housing/utility charges     0.0    (0.0)    +2.3    (2.1)</p>
<p>    Furniture			 0.0   (-0.1)    +0.9    (1.3)</p>
<p>    Health services		+0.2   (0.2)     +3.0    (2.8)</p>
<p>    Transportation		  0.0    (0.4)    +3.0    (2.9)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture  +0.2   (-1.2)    +1.0    (0.9)</p>
<p>    Education			 0.0    (0.0)    +4.1    (4.1)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants     +0.8    (0.1)    +2.6    (2.7)</p>
<p>    Other goods and services   +0.4    (1.2)    +3.2    (3.5)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129507</p>
